          "explanation": "The five interior linemen are ineligible. The tight end and X are on the ends of the line, and Z, H, the running back and the shotgun quarterback are in the backfield, so all of them are eligible.",
          "concept": "ineligible-receiver"
        },
        {
          "type": "true_false",
          "id": "a2-eligibility-05",
          "statement": "In the NFL, an offensive tackle can catch a pass if he reports to the referee as eligible and lines up at an eligible spot.",
          "answer": true,
          "explanation": "High school and college don't allow it. NFL teams use this near the goal line: a lineman reports eligible and lines up as a tight end.",
          "concept": "ineligible-receiver"
        },
        {
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "id": "a2-eligibility-06",
          "prompt": "A guard runs 5 yards downfield before a pass is thrown over the line. What is the call?",
          "choices": [
            "Ineligible receiver downfield",
            "Holding",
            "Pass interference",
            "Illegal motion"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Ineligible players may not drift more than a yard downfield before a forward pass beyond the line is thrown. In the NFL it is a 5-yard penalty.",
          "concept": "ineligible-receiver"
        },
        {
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "id": "a2-eligibility-07",
          "prompt": "The offense snaps the ball with six players on the line. What happens?",
          "choices": [
            "Illegal formation, 5 yards",
            "Nothing, six is enough",
            "Offside on the defense",
            "Loss of down"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Seven must be on the line. Six is an illegal formation.",
          "concept": "line-of-scrimmage"
        },
        {
          "type": "true_false",
          "id": "a2-eligibility-08",
          "statement": "A team may throw two forward passes on one play if both are thrown from behind the line of scrimmage.",
          "answer": false,
          "explanation": "Only one forward pass is allowed per play, and only from behind the line. Backward passes (laterals) are allowed anywhere, any number of times.",
          "concept": "pass-play"
        },
        {
          "type": "true_false",
          "id": "a2-eligibility-09",
          "statement": "Offside is called when a defender is across the line of scrimmage as the ball is snapped.",
          "answer": true,
          "explanation": "Offside is 5 yards. A defender who gets back before the snap without contact has no foul.",
          "concept": "offside"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a2-motion",
      "title": "Motion and Shifts",
      "blurb": "Moving before the snap.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "id": "a2-motion-01",
          "title": "Motion",
          "body": "One offensive player may be moving at the snap, as long as he is moving parallel to the line or away from it, never toward it.",
          "concept": "motion"
        },
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "id": "a2-motion-02",
          "title": "Shifts",
          "body": "When several players change position before the snap, that is a shift. Afterwards everyone must be set for a full second before the ball is snapped.",
          "concept": "shift"
        },
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "id": "a2-motion-03",
          "title": "Why move?",
          "body": "Motion changes the picture for the defense. If a defender runs across the field with the man in motion, that hints at man coverage; if the defense just slides over, that hints at zone.",
          "concept": "motion"
        },
        {
          "type": "true_false",
          "id": "a2-motion-04",
          "statement": "Two offensive players can be in motion at the snap.",
          "answer": false,
          "explanation": "Only one player may be in motion when the ball is snapped.",
          "concept": "motion"
        },
        {
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "id": "a2-motion-05",
          "prompt": "A receiver in motion is moving toward the line of scrimmage at the snap. What is the call?",
          "choices": [
            "Illegal motion",
            "Offside",
            "False start",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Motion must be parallel to the line or away from it. Moving forward at the snap is illegal motion.",
          "concept": "motion"
        },
        {
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "id": "a2-motion-06",
          "prompt": "A cornerback runs across the formation, following the receiver in motion. What does that suggest?",
          "choices": [
            "Man coverage",
            "Zone coverage",
            "A blitz is impossible",
            "A punt"
